---
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Sam Lau - UC San Diego</title>
</head>
<body class="pi-body">
  <div class="pi-page">
    <div class="pi-container">
      <header class="pi-header">
        <a href="/" class="wordmark">Sam Lau</a>
        <nav class="pi-nav" aria-label="Primary">
          <a href="#home" aria-current="page">Home</a>
          <a href="#research">Research</a>
          <a href="#teaching">Teaching</a>
          <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <main id="home">
        <section class="intro-panel" aria-labelledby="page-title">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Halıcıoğlu Data Science Institute / UC San Diego</p>
            <h1 id="page-title">Computing education, data science tools, and human-centered programming systems.</h1>
          </div>
          <img src="/sam_lau_headshot_small.JPG" alt="Sam Lau" class="headshot" width="144" height="144" />
        </section>

        <p class="mission">
          I am an Assistant Teaching Professor at UC San Diego. I apply methods
          from human-computer interaction to design software tools for education,
          with a focus on helping students learn data science and programming.
          I authored <a href="https://learningds.org/">Learning Data Science</a>,
          published by O'Reilly Media in 2023.
        </p>

        <section id="research" class="timeline" aria-label="Research and work">
          <article class="entry entry-featured">
            <div class="entry-heading">
              <h2><a href="https://pandastutor.com/">Pandas Tutor</a></h2>
              <time>Project</time>
            </div>
            <p>
              Step-by-step diagrams showing how Python pandas code transforms
              data, designed to make table operations easier to inspect and teach.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry entry-plain">
            <div class="entry-heading">
              <h2>Barriers that Programming Instructors Face While Performing Emergency Pedagogical Design</h2>
              <time>CHI 2026</time>
            </div>
            <p>How instructors shape student-AI interactions with generative AI tools.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry entry-plain">
            <div class="entry-heading">
              <h2>Improving LLM-Generated Educational Content</h2>
              <time>SIGCSE 2026</time>
            </div>
            <p>Methods for improving the quality of AI-generated materials for computing education.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry entry-featured">
            <div class="entry-heading">
              <h2>Designing and Implementing Skill Tests at Scale</h2>
              <time>SIGCSE 2026</time>
            </div>
            <p>
              Assessment infrastructure and pedagogy for practice-oriented data
              science courses with many students.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry entry-plain">
            <div class="entry-heading">
              <h2>The Design Space of LLM-Based AI Coding Assistants</h2>
              <time>VL/HCC 2025</time>
            </div>
            <p>A map of interaction patterns and tradeoffs for AI tools that help people program.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry entry-plain">
            <div class="entry-heading">
              <h2>How Novices Use Program Visualizations</h2>
              <time>SIGCSE 2025</time>
            </div>
            <p>Evidence about how learners interpret visual explanations while programming.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="entry entry-featured">
            <div class="entry-heading">
              <h2>Learning Data Science</h2>
              <time>O'Reilly 2023</time>
            </div>
            <p>
              A practical textbook for working with data using modern Python,
              statistical reasoning, and exploratory analysis.
            </p>
          </article>
        </section>

        <section id="teaching" class="teaching-section">
          <h2>Teaching</h2>
          <div class="course-list">
            <p><strong>DSC 80</strong> Practice and Application of Data Science</p>
            <p><strong>DSC 106</strong> Data Visualization</p>
            <p><strong>Data 100</strong> Principles and Techniques of Data Science</p>
            <p><strong>Data 8</strong> Foundations of Data Science</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="contact" class="contact-section">
          <p>
            I work with the <a href="https://dstl-lab.github.io/">DSTL Lab</a>
            on tools for data science teaching and learning.
          </p>
          <p class="contact-links">
            <a href="mailto:lau@ucsd.edu">lau@ucsd.edu</a>
            <a href="/cv">CV</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/samlau95">GitHub</a>
            <a href="https://twitter.com/samlau95">Twitter</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </main>

      <footer class="pi-footer">
        <p>Sam Lau</p>
        <span>UC San Diego</span>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>

<style>
  .pi-body {
    margin: 0;
    min-height: 100vh;
    background: #f8f7ef;
    color: #171717;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "SF Mono", Consolas, "Liberation Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  .pi-page {
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .pi-container {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .pi-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .wordmark {
    color: #171717;
    font-family: Georgia, Cambria, "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
    font-size: 1.875rem;
    line-height: 1.05;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .pi-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .pi-nav a {
    color: #171717;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.45rem;
    transition: color 150ms ease, text-decoration-thickness 150ms ease;
  }

  .pi-nav a:not([aria-current="page"]) {
    color: #777568;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }

  .pi-nav a:hover {
    color: #171717;
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  .intro-panel {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  h1,
  h2,
  p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: #777568;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 34rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .headshot {
    width: 4.25rem;
    height: 4.25rem;
    border: 1px solid #171717;
    box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #171717;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.08);
  }

  .mission {
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  a {
    color: #171717;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.18rem;
  }

  a:hover {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }

  .timeline {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 0 1rem 1.75rem;
    border-left: 1px solid #d4d3cb;
  }

  .timeline::before,
  .timeline::after {
    position: absolute;
    left: -1px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1.5rem;
    content: "";
  }

  .timeline::before {
    top: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to top, transparent, #f8f7ef);
  }

  .timeline::after {
    bottom: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, #f8f7ef);
  }

  .entry {
    position: relative;
  }

  .entry::before {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.75rem;
    left: -2.03rem;
    width: 0.45rem;
    height: 0.45rem;
    border-radius: 0.1rem;
    background: #171717;
    outline: 2px solid #f8f7ef;
    content: "";
  }

  .entry-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .entry h2,
  .teaching-section h2 {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    color: #171717;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }

  .entry time {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: #777568;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .entry p {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
    color: #777568;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }

  .entry-featured {
    padding: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid #171717;
    background: #ffffff;
    box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #171717;
    transition: box-shadow 150ms ease, transform 150ms ease;
  }

  .entry-featured:hover {
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 #171717;
    transform: translate(-1px, -1px);
  }

  .entry-plain {
    padding: 0.55rem 0.75rem;
  }

  .entry-plain:hover {
    background: #efeee5;
  }

  .teaching-section,
  .contact-section {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .course-list {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .contact-section p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
  }

  .pi-footer {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid #171717;
  }

  .pi-footer p {
    font-family: Georgia, Cambria, "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .pi-footer span {
    color: #777568;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .pi-page {
      padding: 3rem;
    }

    .pi-header {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .intro-panel {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .headshot {
      grid-row: 1;
      margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    }

    .entry-heading {
      display: block;
    }

    .entry time {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 0.2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
